# The push venue of the gauntlet (ADR-0010).
#
# Unlike the two in-session venues this one refuses, and it fails closed: a gauntlet that cannot
# run its checks refuses the push rather than waving it through, because unlike a hook mid-turn
# there is a human here who can fix it, and the next thing downstream of this is `main`.
#
# It installs itself. `"prepare": "husky"` plus `npm ci` means the runner and any fresh clone get
# this hook without anyone remembering to run a setup step — so an agent's pushes meet the same
# gate the owner's do. That is the whole reason it is worth having a venue here at all.
#
# `--no-verify` still skips it, and that gap is accepted rather than open: branch protection would
# close it and the purchase is declined (ADR-0071).
#
# `npm run check` rather than `bin/gauntlet push` directly, because the push venue is now the
# gauntlet *plus* the clone gate: the gate is too slow for the turn-end venue and the gauntlet runs
# the same `test` slot at both, so it is scheduled beside the gauntlet rather than inside it
# (docs/agents/clone-gate.md rule 6). `check` is the `all` slot of `.claude/contract.json` — one
# spelling of the full green gate, which is what this venue owes `main`.

npm run check
